      "definition_text": {
        "text": "Reference types do not store the actual values; they store a reference (address) to an object somewhere in memory. Variables of a reference type hold this address, so different variables can point to the same object, and changes via one variable are visible through the others.",
        "refs": ["Q0026", "Q0027", "Q0028", "Q0029", "Q0031"],
